    {"start": 7.505, "end": 11.345, "lines": ["Wonderful words. Thanks, George.","Good afternoon, everyone."]},
    {"start": 11.345, "end": 15.105, "lines": ["We are here at Kennedy Space Center","after another incredible launch."]},
    {"start": 15.105, "end": 18.945, "lines": ["So at 11:10 a.m. Eastern Time,","Crew 13 successfully launched"]},
    {"start": 18.945, "end": 22.465, "lines": ["on a SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket","from Launch Complex 40"]},
    {"start": 22.465, "end": 26.976, "lines": ["at the Cape Canaveral Space","Force Station here in Florida."]},
    {"start": 26.976, "end": 28.336, "lines": ["So Jessica, Luke, Josh,"]},
    {"start": 28.336, "end": 31.456, "lines": ["and Sergei are safely in orbit.","They are out of their suits"]},
    {"start": 31.456, "end": 35.296, "lines": ["at this time. And because of the short","phasing period, the crew are going to"]},
    {"start": 35.296, "end": 38.496, "lines": ["have an opportunity to rest","up a little bit before rendezvousing"]},
    {"start": 38.496, "end": 42.496, "lines": ["with the International Space Station.","All in orbit checkouts are complete,"]},
    {"start": 42.496, "end": 44.656, "lines": ["and Dragon is healthy."]},
    {"start": 44.656, "end": 45.696, "lines": ["It was an incredible"]},
    {"start": 45.696, "end": 49.296, "lines": ["launch. I'd like to thank all of those","who contribute to it, right from the"]},
    {"start": 49.296, "end": 50.736, "lines": ["top with our President, President"]},
    {"start": 50.736, "end": 54.336, "lines": ["Trump, all the way through congressional","leadership like Congressman Herodopoulos"]},
    {"start": 54.336, "end": 55.616, "lines": ["was here for the launch."]},
    {"start": 55.616, "end": 58.016, "lines": ["We had representatives from the CSA,"]},
    {"start": 58.016, "end": 62.016, "lines": ["the entire NASA workforce that goes","into making a mission like this possible."]},
    {"start": 62.016, "end": 66.096, "lines": ["Of course, our commercial crew partner,","SpaceX, Space Force, again,"]},
    {"start": 66.096, "end": 68.528, "lines": ["everyone that contributed today.","I'd also like"]},
    {"start": 68.528, "end": 72.288, "lines": ["to especially thank the crew's families","that they've left behind in service"]},
    {"start": 72.288, "end": 76.928, "lines": ["to their nation, to science, and really","for the benefit of all humankind."]},
    {"start": 76.928, "end": 78.048, "lines": ["It was not that long"]},
    {"start": 78.048, "end": 82.128, "lines": ["ago that the shuttle program ended","and America entered a dark period."]},
    {"start": 82.128, "end": 87.888, "lines": ["For nearly a decade, we could not launch","our own astronauts from U.S. soil."]},
    {"start": 87.888, "end": 91.168, "lines": ["Then during President Trump's first term,","we had Demo 2,"]},
    {"start": 91.168, "end": 94.768, "lines": ["which returned human spaceflight","to the space coast where it belongs."]},
    {"start": 94.768, "end": 97.264, "lines": ["And just six years later, here we are."]},
    {"start": 97.264, "end": 99.744, "lines": ["With Crew 13 already underway."]},
    {"start": 99.744, "end": 103.584, "lines": ["And I said earlier today that missions","like this have become so reliable"]},
    {"start": 103.584, "end": 107.184, "lines": ["that they can almost feel routine,","but they are not."]},
    {"start": 107.184, "end": 109.984, "lines": ["Putting human beings on top","of a rocket and accelerating"]},
    {"start": 109.984, "end": 114.224, "lines": ["them to 17,500 miles per hour,","rendezvousing with a space station"]},
    {"start": 114.224, "end": 118.624, "lines": ["and then bringing them home safely many,","many months later will never be routine."]},
    {"start": 118.624, "end": 120.272, "lines": ["These are demanding missions."]},
    {"start": 120.272, "end": 125.872, "lines": ["They take dedication, extreme expertise","and competence across thousands of people"]},
    {"start": 125.872, "end": 128.352, "lines": ["from NASA, the Space Force, and again,"]},
    {"start": 128.352, "end": 133.232, "lines": ["our industry partners like SpaceX","to pull them off very successfully."]},
    {"start": 133.232, "end": 136.992, "lines": ["But building that capability,","the experience, and confidence"]},
    {"start": 136.992, "end": 138.352, "lines": ["to do it repeatedly,"]},
    {"start": 138.352, "end": 142.352, "lines": ["to make it look near routine,","is exactly what we're collectively"]},
    {"start": 142.352, "end": 144.832, "lines": ["striving to achieve.","Now, because of the bravery"]},
    {"start": 144.832, "end": 146.992, "lines": ["of this incredible crew and our amazing"]},
    {"start": 146.992, "end": 151.008, "lines": ["astronaut corps, There will be children","watching today who will never know a time"]},
    {"start": 151.008, "end": 153.888, "lines": ["when America could not launch","its own astronauts to space."]},
    {"start": 153.888, "end": 157.488, "lines": ["They watched Artemis II travel","around the moon, they watched Crew 13"]},
    {"start": 157.488, "end": 161.728, "lines": ["today launch to space, and before long,","they will watch astronauts return"]},
    {"start": 161.728, "end": 165.648, "lines": ["to the lunar surface to see the beginnings","of a moon base take shape, to grow"]},
    {"start": 165.648, "end": 170.128, "lines": ["up in a country where there's a United","States Space Academy and someday tune"]},
    {"start": 170.128, "end": 174.368, "lines": ["in to watch their favorite astronaut","set foot on a planet other than our own."]},
    {"start": 174.368, "end": 175.648, "lines": ["Now, this crew will turn"]},
    {"start": 175.648, "end": 179.6, "lines": ["their attention. In the hours ahead","to rendezvous and docking, and then months"]},
    {"start": 179.6, "end": 183.2, "lines": ["of important work aboard the International","Space Station that will benefit"]},
    {"start": 183.2, "end": 186.56, "lines": ["life here at home and help prepare","future crews for their missions"]},
    {"start": 186.56, "end": 191.04, "lines": ["to the moon, Mars, and someday beyond.","This is an absolute great start to Crew"]},
    {"start": 191.04, "end": 194.96, "lines": ["13. We'll be watching very closely,","cheering them on throughout their great"]},
    {"start": 194.96, "end": 197.6, "lines": ["expedition. And now I will hand","it over to our Associate"]},
    {"start": 197.6, "end": 201.2, "lines": ["Administrator of Human Space Flight","Mission Directorate, Dr. Lori Glaze. Lori?"]},
    {"start": 201.2, "end": 202.36, "lines": ["Thank you, Jared."]}
  ]
}
